ld be to pass.\n", "output": "Evaluation: [Pass]\nReason: Penging B3 creates a Pung but leaves the hand with only three complete melds (Chi T1-T2-T3, Pung B3, and Chow W3-W4-W5) and a pair of T9s, which is insufficient for a valid winning hand. Passing preserves flexibility to potentially form additional melds or pairs later. The remaining tiles (T8, T9, B1, B4) lack structure for a fourth meld, making Peng B3 suboptimal at this stage.\nAnswer: Pass"}
